# ============================================================================
# Redis Cloud Configuration (redis.io)
# ============================================================================
#
# Redis Cloud provides managed Redis instances with high availability
# and low latency. This configuration uses Redis Cloud in ap-south-1 region.
#
# Setup Instructions:
# 1. Sign up at https://redis.io/cloud/ (free tier available)
# 2. Create a new Redis database
# 3. Select region: ap-south-1 (AWS Mumbai) for lowest latency
# 4. Copy the connection details from the Redis Cloud console
# 5. Add these environment variables to your .env.local file
#
# Required Environment Variables:
REDIS_HOST=redis-xxxxx.c301.ap-south-1-1.ec2.redns.redis-cloud.com
REDIS_PORT=17948
REDIS_PASSWORD=your-redis-password-here

# Note: If Redis credentials are not provided, the application will
# automatically fall back to in-memory caching (not recommended for production)

